/// known-gap: interp keeps the old behaviour (drops `order: 5` quietly); the interpreter is being retired
/// In a class, `order:` sets the order its objects make their decisions
/// in, so `order` is never a field: giving it when making an object is
/// R0413, not a value quietly dropped (owner, 2026-11-09).
<>Land |
    size: 1
    order: @size
xx
a <> Land | size: 2, order: 5
say(a)
